From: cengine maintainers
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] fuse: opt-in pending-request credential snapshots

Linux 6.18.44, after 0001. Not in the production series. GPL-2.0-only
kernel modifications; UAPI retains its Linux-syscall-note exception.

Pin immutable current credentials on ordinary task request allocation and
query only the delivering device's existing processing queue. No PID lookup,
no persistent unique-ID registry, no implicit root for synthesized requests.
Native init-user-namespace mounts only; no idmapped mounts, virtiofs, CUSE,
FUSE-over-io_uring or passthrough. This is a credential gate prototype, not
a storage backend or complete Linux security-context transport.
ABI v3 also snapshots effective capabilities; managed_close_to_open opts
native FUSE into the existing checked buffered-cache reopen sequence.

ABI v3 preserves managed SETATTR intent. A separate privileged-minted anonymous
storage session applies trusted metadata on local ext4 under CURRENT credentials,
without requiring a FUSE connection or a source request in the storage kernel.

